  gonna have to think about this because  obviously you know  everybody loves angela because she's  amazing and i was getting you know  contacted by various people and we were  getting encouraged  you know to do this so we wanted to make  sure that what we did was together  because we thought that together  as a joint ticket a leader and a deputy  because we're so close  we're close but slightly different you  know in terms of the way we operate and  the way we are  we thought we would be a really positive  unifying force  for the parliamentary labour party for  our membership  and also send a positive message out to  the country after  years of division quite frankly and  quite fractious politics that  politics does not have to be nasty  talking about um fractious  debates i've got to get your view on the  big debate at the moment  harry and megan where'd you stand how do  you make it about whether they leave the  uk or not  i don't want them to leave the uk but  i'll be honest i mean  megan you know she's talked about  hostility from you know all the kind of  sections of the press i mean certainly  one of the things i've witnessed in in  my  kind of early days of my campaign this  was even before i decided to stand as  leader  were the levels of abuse and the fact  that i was getting targeted above all  the other candidates for some reason  and and it seemed quite hostile and you  know i think she's faced  you know horrific abuse within the press  and that's not acceptable you know  sexism i think certainly you know  male counterparts don't receive the same  level of hostility  and i think the media has a job to make  sure that it is balanced  it is looking at the facts of course you  know report facts and attack where you  can see that there are misdemeanors  wrongdoings or inaccuracies  but don't attack a woman for the sake of  attacking a woman just finally  can you clear it up is there a hyphen in  long bay or not there's actually there  actually is a hyphen  